{
  "mn131:0.1": "Middle Discourses 131 ",
  "mn131:0.2": "One Fine Night ",
  "mn131:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn131:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn131:1.3": "There the Buddha addressed the mendicants, ",
  "mn131:1.4": "“Mendicants!” ",
  "mn131:1.5": "“Venerable sir,” they replied. ",
  "mn131:1.6": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "mn131:2.1": "“I shall teach you the summary recital and the analysis of the one who has one fine night. ",
  "mn131:2.2": "Listen and apply your mind well, I will speak.” ",
  "mn131:2.3": "“Yes, sir,” they replied. ",
  "mn131:2.4": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "mn131:3.1": "“Don’t run back to the past, ",
  "mn131:3.2": "don’t anticipate the future. ",
  "mn131:3.3": "What’s past is left behind, ",
  "mn131:3.4": "the future has not arrived; ",
  "mn131:3.5": "and any present phenomenon ",
  "mn131:3.6": "you clearly discern in every case. ",
  "mn131:3.7": "The unfaltering, the unshakable: ",
  "mn131:3.8": "having known that, foster it. ",
  "mn131:3.9": "Today’s the day to keenly work—",
  "mn131:3.10": "who knows, tomorrow may bring death! ",
  "mn131:3.11": "For there is no bargain to be struck ",
  "mn131:3.12": "with Death and his mighty horde. ",
  "mn131:3.13": "One who keenly meditates like this, ",
  "mn131:3.14": "tireless all night and day: ",
  "mn131:3.15": "that’s who has one fine night—",
  "mn131:3.16": "so declares the peaceful sage. ",
  "mn1